# Cloudflare Pages routing rules.
#
# Cross-origin 200 proxy is NOT supported by _redirects on Cloudflare
# Pages — only same-origin proxy works here. The backend-bound paths
# (/sitemap.xml, /llms-full.txt, /cities-index.html, /cawm-tiles/*)
# are handled by Pages Functions in the functions/ directory instead.
#
# Do NOT add a /about -> /about.html redirect here. Cloudflare Pages
# already auto-redirects /about.html -> /about (308, built-in "pretty
# URL" canonicalization for static .html files) and serves the file's
# content at the extensionless path. An explicit reverse rule fights
# that behavior and produces an infinite /about <-> /about.html loop
# (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS) — this was live in prod for a few minutes
# on 2026-08-06, reverted here.
#
# This file only contains the SPA fallback: any unknown path serves
# the React app's index.html so client-side routing
# (/cities/:country/:city, /panel, /reset-password, /auth/callback)
# works on hard refresh. Functions take precedence over this rule.
/*  /index.html  200
